% formalizes: claim:ethics-a3
% claim: Axiom III: from a definite cause an effect necessarily follows, and without one no effect can
% says: From a given definite cause an effect necessarily follows; and, on the other hand, if no definite cause be granted, it is impossible that an effect can follow.
% The first half, "from a definite cause an effect necessarily follows",
% needs an existential in the head. The second half: an effect has a cause.
has_cause(E) :- cause_of(_, E).
bottom :- effect(E), not has_cause(E).
